## Learning objectives
- Differentiate Revocable vs Irrevocable Trusts
- Apply updated Capital Gains rules

## What is it?
Level 2 advisory focuses on advanced financial architecture: estate preservation, inter-generational wealth transfer via private trusts, complex tax optimization, and post-retirement wealth management.

## Why it matters
High-Net-Worth Individuals (HNIs) require sophisticated structures to protect family wealth from commercial claims, family disputes, and tax leakage.

## How it works
Advisers design Private Discretionary Trusts where assets are held by trustees for designated beneficiaries with clear distribution covenants.

## Key definitions
- **Private Discretionary Trust** - A trust where trustees have discretion over the timing and proportion of distributions to beneficiaries, shielding assets from individual creditor claims.
- **Probate** - The official certification of a Will granted by a court of competent jurisdiction.

## Rules & regulations
- There is currently zero estate duty or inheritance tax in India.
- Assets received under a valid Will or by way of inheritance are exempt from income tax in the hands of the recipient.

## Practical scenario
An aging entrepreneur wants to ensure his special-needs daughter is financially protected for life without interference from extended relatives. An advisor structures an Irrevocable Private Family Trust with institutional co-trustees.

## Common mistakes
- Thinking a Will avoids probate automatically; probate is mandatory for Wills executed in presidential towns (Mumbai, Kolkata, Chennai).

